# Bumelerze — local environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and paste in the values below.
# `.env` is git-ignored (see .gitignore) — never commit real values.
#
# Four values. The two Supabase values switch the app from local-only mode
# (felt reports, check-ins and feedback stay queued on the device; no
# telemetry ping is sent) to fully wired (everything syncs to Supabase). The
# MapTiler and VAPID keys are optional. No other code change is required —
# see supabase/README.md "How the app connects". The production web build
# sets all four in scripts/build-app-web.sh.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables are inlined into the JS bundle by Expo/
# Metro at build time (the standard Expo SDK 57 pattern — no app.config.ts
# change needed). They are visible in the built app bundle, which is exactly
# right for the anon key (it's meant to be public; every RLS policy in
# supabase/migrations/ is written assuming the anon key is not a secret).
# Never put a service_role key in an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable.

# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional — Map tab (web) basemap quality upgrade. Leave unset and the map
# uses OpenFreeMap (free, no key, no signup) automatically; this is a pure
# quality bump, never required for the app to work. Get a free key at
# https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/ and paste it below to switch the
# Map tab to MapTiler's `outdoor-v4` (light) and `outdoor-v4-dark` (dark)
# styles, both with real terrain-relief cartography — see
# `src/features/map/style-provider.ts` for the exact style ids and how they
# were verified. If the MapTiler style ever fails to load at runtime (bad
# key, quota), the app automatically falls back to OpenFreeMap — the map
# never goes blank either way.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=

# Optional — earthquake alerts by web push (migration 0062). The PUBLIC VAPID
# key the browser subscribes with; the matching private key lives only in the
# send-alerts Edge Function secrets. Leave unset and the alert controls say
# alerts are not set up in this build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iOS/Android builds only. Read by app.config.ts (not inlined into the app's
# JavaScript); leave empty until the Expo account exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Expo account: after `eas init`, the account (or organisation) name and the
# project id it prints. With the project id set, the native app also gets its
# EAS Update address (fixes reach installed apps without a store release).
EXPO_OWNER=
EAS_PROJECT_ID=
